   NOTE: The user mentioned "pdfplumber" but that is a Python library. PdfPig is the correct
   100% C# equivalent with the same Apache-2.0 license philosophy. Use PdfPig.
7. **Excel export**: Use **ClosedXML** (NuGet: `ClosedXML`) — MIT licensed. No EPPlus
   (commercial for v5+).
8. **Database**: SQLite via **Microsoft.Data.Sqlite** (MIT) + **Entity Framework Core 10** with
   the `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite` provider (MIT).
9. **Web framework**: ASP.NET Core 10 with Razor Pages + minimal API endpoints.
   No Blazor, no React frontend, no external JS framework required — vanilla JS + Tailwind CDN
   is acceptable for UI.
10. **Image processing for scanned/amended PDFs**: Use **SkiaSharp** (NuGet: `SkiaSharp`) — MIT
    licensed, for rendering PDF pages to bitmaps before passing to PaddleOCR.
    Use `Sdcb.PdfiumRenderer` (Apache-2.0) for PDF-to-image rendering.
11. **Amended PDF handling**: PDFs edited with Foxit Fill & Sign (or similar tools) that use
    white-box overlays to cover original text MUST be routed to the OCR path, never the digital
    text extraction path. This is enforced by the Conflict Resolution Engine described below.
    This rule is safety-critical — a false negative (reading ghost/hidden text instead of the
    amended visible text) is unacceptable in an aerospace context.
12. **PaddleSharp model loading**: The OCR model MUST be loaded from a local bundled path only.
    Never allow automatic internet download of model files at runtime. The server may be
    air-gapped. Model download failure must produce a clear startup error, not a silent crash.
13. **Memory management**: Every `SKBitmap`, `SKImage`, and PdfiumRenderer page object MUST be
    disposed immediately after use. Do not accumulate bitmaps in memory across pages.
14. **Idempotency**: Re-running extraction on the same folder must never create duplicate records.
    Enforce via SHA-256 file hash deduplication before processing any file.
15. **Input path security**: Never process a folder path that has not been validated against an
    explicit allowlist defined in appsettings.json. Reject path traversal attempts.

