## BACKGROUND: WHY CERTAIN DESIGN DECISIONS ARE MANDATORY

### Amended PDF Detection
When a user edits a PDF using Foxit Fill & Sign by placing white rectangles over existing text
and typing new text on top, the PDF file internally retains BOTH the original text objects AND
the new overlay text. PDF text extractors (including PdfPig) read ALL text objects from the
content stream regardless of visual stacking order. This means a naive digital extractor returns
BOTH old (hidden) and new (visible) text, producing corrupted data rows. The Conflict Resolution
Engine routes amended files to OCR, which renders only the visible layer — exactly what a human
sees.

### OCR Table Column Order
PaddleOCR detects text regions independently and returns them in detection order, not
left-to-right table reading order. For a 12-column tooling table, this means columns will
frequently be returned out of sequence unless results are explicitly sorted by bounding box
X coordinate within each Y-grouped line. This must be enforced in the extractor, not patched
in the parser.

### File Hash Deduplication
Without SHA-256 deduplication, re-running the same folder (e.g. after adding one new file)
doubles all previously extracted records in SQLite. This is silent data corruption. The hash
check must happen before the PDF classifier, before OCR, before any I/O on the file content.

### PaddleSharp Offline Model
PaddleSharp's LocalFullModels calls attempt to download model weights from the internet on
first use. An aerospace facility server is commonly air-gapped or has outbound HTTP blocked by
firewall. The application must bundle the PP-OCRv4 model files in `./models/ppocr_v4/` and
load them explicitly from that local path on every startup.

### SQLite Write Contention
SQLite permits only one concurrent writer. With 4 parallel file workers all calling
SaveChangesAsync simultaneously, intermittent SQLiteBusyException will occur. All parallel
workers must collect records into a ConcurrentBag and a dedicated single writer thread must
perform batch inserts, never concurrent DbContext writes.

### Path Traversal Security
The web UI accepts a folder path string from the user. Without validation, any path on the
server filesystem (including system directories or network shares) could be read. All accepted
paths must be checked against an AllowedBasePaths whitelist in appsettings.json before any
file enumeration begins.

