## STARTUP VALIDATION SERVICE

### StartupValidationService.cs

This service runs at application startup BEFORE the web host begins accepting requests.
If any check fails, the application must refuse to start with a clear human-readable error.

```
Implement IHostedService. Register as hosted service in Program.cs.
Run all checks in StartAsync(). On failure: log the error and call
Environment.Exit(1) after a 2-second delay to allow the log to flush.

CHECK 1 — AVX2 CPU Support:
  Use System.Runtime.Intrinsics.X86.Avx2.IsSupported.
  If false:
    Log.Fatal("STARTUP FAILURE: This server's CPU does not support AVX2 instructions,
    which are required by PaddleSharp MKL-DNN inference. Minimum requirement: Intel
    Haswell (2013) or AMD Ryzen (2017) or newer. Current CPU: {Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("PROCESSOR_IDENTIFIER")}");
    Exit(1).

CHECK 2 — PaddleOCR Model Files Present:
  Read PaddleOcrModelPath from appsettings.json (ToolingExtractor:PaddleOcrModelPath).
  Check that the following files exist under that path:
    - inference.pdmodel
    - inference.pdiparams
  If any are missing:
    Log.Fatal("STARTUP FAILURE: PaddleOCR model files not found at '{path}'.
    Download PP-OCRv4 English model files and place them in the models/ppocr_v4/ directory.
    See models/ppocr_v4/README.md for download instructions. The application will NOT
    attempt to download model files automatically.");
    Exit(1).

CHECK 3 — Allowed Base Paths Configured:
  Read AllowedBasePaths from appsettings.json (ToolingExtractor:AllowedBasePaths).
  If the list is empty or null:
    Log.Fatal("STARTUP FAILURE: No AllowedBasePaths configured in appsettings.json.
    Add at least one allowed folder path under ToolingExtractor:AllowedBasePaths.
    The application will not accept any folder extraction requests without this.");
    Exit(1).

CHECK 4 — Required Output Directories:
  Create the following directories if they do not exist:
    ./data/
    ./amended_pdf_log/
    ./failed_extractions/
  If creation fails (permissions error):
    Log.Fatal("STARTUP FAILURE: Cannot create output directory '{dir}': {ex.Message}");
    Exit(1).

CHECK 5 — SQLite Database Accessible:
  Attempt to open the SQLite connection and run a simple SELECT 1.
  If it fails:
    Log.Fatal("STARTUP FAILURE: Cannot access SQLite database at '{path}': {ex.Message}");
    Exit(1).
```

