## IMAGE PRE-PROCESSING PIPELINE

### ImagePreprocessor.cs

This class is called by ScannedPdfExtractor on every rendered bitmap BEFORE passing to
PaddleOCR. It addresses low-quality scans (fax scans, skewed pages, low contrast).

```csharp
public class ImagePreprocessor
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Applies deskew, contrast enhancement, and binarization to improve OCR accuracy
    /// on low-quality scans. Returns a new SKBitmap — caller must dispose both bitmaps.
    /// </summary>
    public SKBitmap Preprocess(SKBitmap source)
    {
        // STEP 1 — Convert to grayscale
        var grayscale = ToGrayscale(source);

        // STEP 2 — Otsu binarization (adaptive threshold)
        // Compute histogram of pixel values, find Otsu threshold,
        // convert each pixel to pure black (< threshold) or white (>= threshold).
        var binarized = OtsuBinarize(grayscale);
        grayscale.Dispose();

        // STEP 3 — Deskew
        // Detect dominant line angle using Hough-like horizontal projection profile.
        // Rotate the bitmap by the detected skew angle (max ±15 degrees).
        // If no clear skew detected (< 0.5 degrees), skip rotation.
        var deskewed = Deskew(binarized);
        binarized.Dispose();

        return deskewed;
    }

    private SKBitmap ToGrayscale(SKBitmap source) { /* SkiaSharp pixel-level grayscale */ }
    private SKBitmap OtsuBinarize(SKBitmap grayscale) { /* Otsu threshold implementation */ }
    private SKBitmap Deskew(SKBitmap binarized) { /* Horizontal projection deskew */ }
}
```

**Important**: Pre-processing is applied ONLY when the source bitmap's average pixel
brightness (mean of all pixels) is below 0.85 (not already a clean white-background image).
For clean digital renders, skip pre-processing entirely to avoid degrading quality.

Record the applied rotation angle in `ToolingRecord.PageOrientation`.

