## PAGE ORIENTATION DETECTION

### In ScannedPdfExtractor.cs — before calling ImagePreprocessor:

```
After rendering each page to bitmap at 300 DPI:
1. Run a lightweight orientation check:
   - Attempt OCR on a small center crop of the bitmap (middle 50% of width/height).
   - If word count returned < 3 and the crop is clearly text-like (high contrast):
     Try rotating the bitmap 90°, 180°, 270° and repeat the center-crop OCR.
   - Select the rotation that yields the highest word count from the center crop.
   - Apply that rotation to the full page bitmap before full OCR.
2. Record the rotation angle in degrees in ToolingRecord.PageOrientation.
3. Log.Information("Page {n} of {file}: rotated {angle}° for orientation correction.");
```

