## OCR TEXT CORRECTOR

### OcrTextCorrector.cs

Applies post-OCR correction rules for known character substitution errors that occur
frequently in tooling data. This runs on ALL OCR output before it reaches the parsers.

```csharp
public class OcrTextCorrector
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Corrects common OCR character substitutions in the context of CNC tooling data.
    /// Operates field-by-field after parsing so corrections are context-aware.
    /// </summary>
    public void CorrectRecord(ToolingRecord record)
    {
        record.ToolNo              = CorrectToolNumber(record.ToolNo);
        record.ToolDiameterD1      = CorrectNumericField(record.ToolDiameterD1);
        record.FluteLengthL1       = CorrectNumericField(record.FluteLengthL1);
        record.ToolExtLengthL2     = CorrectNumericField(record.ToolExtLengthL2);
        record.ToolCornerRadius    = CorrectNumericField(record.ToolCornerRadius);
        record.ToolPathTimeMinutes = CorrectNumericField(record.ToolPathTimeMinutes);
        record.PartNumber          = CorrectPartNumber(record.PartNumber);
        record.Operation           = CorrectOperationCode(record.Operation);
        record.Revision            = CorrectRevisionCode(record.Revision);
    }

    // Tool numbers: format is T## or similar — digits only after 'T'
    // Replace: O→0, I→1, l→1, B→8 in the numeric portion only
    private string CorrectToolNumber(string value) { ... }

    // Numeric fields: diameter, length — should be decimal numbers
    // Replace: O→0, I→1, l→1, B→8, S→5, Z→2
    // Normalise decimal separator: comma → period (e.g. "8,5" → "8.5")
    // Remove non-numeric chars except '.' and '-'
    private string CorrectNumericField(string value) { ... }

    // Part numbers: alphanumeric with dashes — correct O/0 ambiguity by context
    // If the character is surrounded by digits → likely 0. If surrounded by letters → likely O.
    private string CorrectPartNumber(string value) { ... }

    // Operation codes: format OPxx — digits after 'OP'
    // Correct: "OP1O" → "OP10", "OPI0" → "OP10"
    private string CorrectOperationCode(string value) { ... }

    // Revision codes: format REVxx — digits after 'REV'
    private string CorrectRevisionCode(string value) { ... }
}
```

**Apply OcrTextCorrector** in ExtractionPipelineService after parsing and before DB insert,
but ONLY when `record.PdfType != PdfType.Digital` (no correction needed for clean text).

