## PARSERS — FULL SPECIFICATION

All parsers implement:
```csharp
public interface IToolingParser
{
    TemplateType SupportedTemplate { get; }
    ExtractionResult Parse(string extractedText, string sourceFile,
                           PdfType pdfType, AmendmentReport? amendmentReport);
}
```

### ParserA.cs — Standard Format

**Header extraction** (regex, IgnoreCase | Multiline):
```
Tool List:\s*(?<toolListId>(?:(?!\n\s*\w+:).)+)          ← captures across line wrap
Part Number:\s*(?<partNumber>[^\n\r]+)
Part Description:\s*(?<partDescription>(?:(?!\n\s*\w+:).)+)
Operation:\s*(?<operation>[^\n\r]+)
Revision:\s*(?<revision>[^\n\r]+)
Project Code:\s*(?<projectCode>[^\n\r]+)
Machine:\s*(?<machine>[^\n\r]+)
Workcenter:\s*(?<workcenter>[^\n\r]+)
Machine Model:\s*(?<machineModel>(?:(?!\n\s*\w+:).)+)
```

Note: `(?:(?!\n\s*\w+:).)+` is a negative lookahead that captures across a line wrap
but stops before the next label (e.g. "Part Description:\nBLEED VALVE\nBODY" where
BODY is a continuation line before the next label). This handles multi-line field values.

Trim all captured values. If not found → `string.Empty`.

**Table extraction**:
1. Find line containing "Tool No." → column header row.
2. Data rows: between column header and footer marker.
   Footer marker regex: `^\s*(CAM Programmer|Approved by|Tool Register)`
3. Skip separator lines (chars `-=_|` repeated ≥ 3).
4. Split each data line by `\t`. If < 3 tokens → attempt merge with next line
   (continuation row detection: if next line also has < 3 tokens, join with space
   and re-split). If still < 3 tokens after merge → skip.
5. Column index map (0-based):
   ```
   0:  ToolNo
   1:  ToolName
   2:  ConsumableToolDescription
   3:  ToolSupplier
   4:  ToolHolder
   5:  ToolDiameterD1
   6:  FluteLengthL1
   7:  ToolExtLengthL2
   8:  ToolCornerRadius
   9:  ArborDescription
   10: ToolPathTimeMinutes
   11: Remarks
   ```
   If index not present → `string.Empty`.
6. Skip rows where ToolNo is empty OR matches the column header text.

**Dynamic header remapping** (robustness against template drift):
Before using the fixed index map, attempt to parse the column header row:
Split by `\t` and build a `Dictionary<string, int>` of columnName → index.
If the header row is found and column names are parseable, use the dynamic map.
Fall back to the fixed index map only if the header row cannot be parsed.
This protects against a CAM programmer inserting a new column between existing ones.

**Footer extraction**:
```
CAM Programmer:\s*(?<camProgrammer>[^\n\r]*)
Approved by:\s*(?<approvedBy>[^\n\r]*)
Tool Register(?:ed)? By:\s*(?<toolRegisteredBy>[^\n\r]*)
```

**Set on every record**:
- `WasAmendmentDetected = (amendmentReport?.IsAmended == true)`
- `AmendmentEvidenceSummary = amendmentReport?.Summary`

### ParserB.cs — Abbreviated Format
Mirror ParserA. Header regex keys: `P/N:`, `OP:`, `W/C:`, `Mach:`, `Model:`.
Use dynamic header remapping always (abbreviated formats vary most in column order).
Propagate amendmentReport to records.

### ParserC.cs — Legacy Format
Header may be comma-delimited single line. Handle both comma and tab.
Column count may be as low as 6. Use dynamic header remapping.
Set `ConfidenceScore = 0.8f` (legacy format uncertainty).
Propagate amendmentReport to records.

### ParserFactory.cs
```csharp
public class ParserFactory
{
    private readonly IEnumerable<IToolingParser> _parsers;
    public ParserFactory(IEnumerable<IToolingParser> parsers) => _parsers = parsers;
    public IToolingParser GetParser(TemplateType type) =>
        _parsers.FirstOrDefault(p => p.SupportedTemplate == type)
        ?? throw new InvalidOperationException($"No parser for template {type}");
}
```

