## EXTRACTION PIPELINE — FULL ORCHESTRATION

### ExtractionPipelineService.cs

```
Method: Task<ExtractionJob> RunAsync(string folderPath, IProgress<int>? progress)

PRE-FLIGHT:
1. FolderScanService.ValidateFolderPath(folderPath) — throws SecurityException if invalid.
2. Create ExtractionJob, save to DB, Status = Running.
3. Enumerate all *.pdf (SearchOption.AllDirectories). Store full paths.
4. Set TotalFiles.

PARALLEL WORKER LOOP (SemaphoreSlim maxDegreeOfParallelism from config, default 4):
For each file:
  a. Compute SHA-256 hash (FileHashService.ComputeSha256).
  b. Query DB: if hash already exists → increment SkippedFiles → continue.
  c. Classify: AmendmentDetector first, then word-count (PdfClassifier).
  d. If Amended → increment AmendedFilesDetected.
  e. Select extractor based on PdfType routing table.
  f. Extract text.
  g. Detect template. If Unknown → copy raw text to failed_extractions/ → increment FailedFiles → continue.
  h. Get parser. Parse with amendmentReport passed through.
  i. Check revision conflicts (query DB for same PartNumber+Operation with different Revision).
     If conflict → log, set RevisionConflictDetected = true on new records, write to revision_conflicts.log.
  j. Add records to ConcurrentBag<ToolingRecord>.
  k. Increment ProcessedFiles, report progress.
  l. Catch per-file exceptions: log full stack trace to errors.log, increment FailedFiles, continue.

SINGLE WRITER AFTER ALL WORKERS COMPLETE:
5. Collect all records from ConcurrentBag.
6. Apply OcrTextCorrector to each record where PdfType != Digital.
7. Bulk insert all records in a single DbContext.SaveChangesAsync() call.
   Retry up to 3 times with 500ms delay on SQLiteBusyException.

8. Update job: Status = Completed, CompletedAt = now.
9. Return job.
```

