### ISSUE 4 — DATA INTEGRITY

#### 4a. Revision Conflict Detection
If `AA000-279_OP10_REV00.pdf` and `AA000-279_OP10_REV01.pdf` are both processed in the same
job, both get inserted into SQLite. There is no constraint preventing conflicting tool lists
for the same part/operation.

**Solution (already mandated in REVISION CONFLICT DETECTION section — verify full compliance)**:
- The pipeline MUST query for existing `(PartNumber, Operation)` with a **different Revision**
  before inserting new records.
- If a conflict is found: set `RevisionConflictDetected = true` on ALL new records from that
  file, log to `revision_conflicts.log` with format:
  `"{Timestamp} | {SourceFile} | {PartNumber} | {Operation} | ExistingRevs: [{revs}] | NewRev: {rev}"`
- Both the old and new revision records remain in the database. The "Review Required" Excel
  sheet surfaces them for manual triage.
- Conflict detection must also run WITHIN the current job batch (ConcurrentBag), not only
  against the DB — two files from the same job folder may conflict with each other.

#### 4b. Re-Running the Same Folder Twice (Idempotency)
Running extraction on the same folder a second time doubles all records in SQLite.

**Solution (already mandated in FILE HASH DEDUPLICATION section — verify full compliance)**:
- SHA-256 dedup check MUST be the very first operation per file — before classification,
  before amendment detection, before any file content read beyond computing the hash.
- Query: `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ToolingRecords WHERE SourceFileHash = @hash`
- If count > 0: increment `job.SkippedFiles`, log, and `continue`. No further processing.
- The `SourceFileHash` index on `ToolingRecord` is mandatory for performance (already in schema).
- Add unit test: `Pipeline_SameFolderTwice_SecondRunSkipsAllFiles`.

#### 4c. SQLite Write Contention Under Parallel Inserts
SQLite has a single writer lock. With 4 parallel workers all calling `SaveChangesAsync()`
simultaneously, intermittent `SQLiteBusyException` will occur.

**Solution (already mandated in EXTRACTION PIPELINE section — verify architecture)**:
- Parallel workers MUST NOT call `DbContext.SaveChangesAsync()` individually.
- Pattern: all workers add to `ConcurrentBag<ToolingRecord>`. After the parallel loop
  completes, a single sequential writer performs one `context.AddRange(allRecords)` +
  `context.SaveChangesAsync()`.
- Retry the single bulk write up to 3 times with 500ms delay on `SqliteException` where
  `SqliteErrorCode == 5` (SQLITE_BUSY) or `SqliteErrorCode == 6` (SQLITE_LOCKED).
- SQLite WAL mode (`Pragma journal_mode=WAL`) must be in the connection string — already
  configured. Verify it is present.

