## BUILD & RUN INSTRUCTIONS (include in README.md)

```
## Prerequisites
- .NET 10 SDK
- Windows x64 (PaddleSharp MKL-DNN — requires AVX2 CPU, Intel Haswell 2013+ or AMD Ryzen+)
  OR Linux x64 with MKLDNN native libs
- CPU with AVX2 support (application will refuse to start and show a clear error if not met)

## Model Setup (required before first run — no internet download at runtime)
1. Download PP-OCRv4 English model from:
   https://paddleocr.bj.bcebos.com/PP-OCRv4/english/en_PP-OCRv4_rec_infer.tar
   https://paddleocr.bj.bcebos.com/PP-OCRv4/english/en_PP-OCRv4_det_infer.tar
2. Extract to: ./models/ppocr_v4/rec/ and ./models/ppocr_v4/det/
3. Verify inference.pdmodel and inference.pdiparams exist in each subfolder.

## Allowed Paths Setup
Edit appsettings.json → ToolingExtractor:AllowedBasePaths.
Add the full path(s) of the folders containing your PDFs.
The app will refuse to process any path not in this list.

## First-time DB setup
dotnet restore
dotnet ef migrations add InitialCreate \
  --project src/ToolingExtractor.Infrastructure \
  --startup-project src/ToolingExtractor.Web
dotnet ef database update \
  --project src/ToolingExtractor.Infrastructure \
  --startup-project src/ToolingExtractor.Web

## Run
dotnet run --project src/ToolingExtractor.Web
# Open http://localhost:5000

## Run tests
dotnet test

## Output directories (auto-created on startup)
./data/                          — SQLite database
./amended_pdf_log/               — JSON reports per detected amended PDF
./failed_extractions/            — Raw text dumps and error logs
./failed_extractions/errors.log  — Per-file error details
./failed_extractions/revision_conflicts.log — Revision conflict audit trail
```

